<title>CANADA: WESTERN CANADA RAIL CAR ALLOCATIONS FOR AUG 8.</title>
<headline>WESTERN CANADA RAIL CAR ALLOCATIONS FOR AUG 8.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Canada's Car Allocation Policy Group on Friday issued its rail car allocations by commodity for loading during shipping week two of the 1997/98 season.</p>
<p>VANCOUVER     2,800 cars</p>
<p>subtotal	2,076 CWB (wheat/barley)</p>
<p>		    510 canola</p>
<p>		     14 oats</p>
<p>PRINCE RUPERT 1,200 CWB</p>
<p>THUNDER BAY   3,000 cars</p>
<p>subtotal	2,779 CWB</p>
<p>			0 canola</p>
<p>		    135 oats</p>
<p>		     86 domestic feed wheat and barley</p>
<p>CHURCHILL	 300 CWB</p>
<p>-does not include U.S.-bound rail cars or interior domestic shipments.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
